          "date": "2026-08-24 13:57:05.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-17000 lfsck: do not fail a scan for a vanished directory",
        "message": "LU-17000 lfsck: do not fail a scan for a vanished directory\n\nGOTO() does not assign its second argument, so the ternary in\nlfsck_namespace_assistant_handler_p1() was discarded and the target\nlabel still saw the -ENOENT that lfsck_assistant_object_load() returns\nwhen the object is already dead. A directory unlinked while the\nnamespace LFSCK was running was therefore logged and counted as an\nLFSCK failure, and with LPF_FAILOUT it aborted the scan.\n\nOne of the four sites jumps to stop:, which falls through to out:.\nThe reload there is guarded by dir == NULL, so the failed load left an\nERR_PTR in dir that could reach lfsck_namespace_repair_bad_name_hash()\nand be dereferenced. Clear dir on that path as well.\n\nAssign the result, spelled as the three working instances of the same\nidiom already in this file.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-lfsck\nFixes: 5b3eef20c5a0 (\"LU-6343 lfsck: locate object only when necessary\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I32953fd4a110d2c0147a4f8cb2962d5337db8d7a\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
